    "brief": "R10-ARCH-DOCS is the LAST stage of round 10 (owner ruling 2026-10-17, tvofi), after every other round-10 group. Its scope was changed by the owner (tvofi, 2026-10-22): the documentation and visualisation are now written early by R10-ARCH-DOCS-FIRST against the protected final shape at programme end. This stage verifies, adjusts and wiring-tests those docs and figures.\n\nAt this stage's merge base, after every listed after-group has merged:\n\n1. Verification:\n   - Check every claim, figure, table, and diagram box and arrow in docs/architecture.md and the developer onboarding (CI shape, orchestration machinery, one handoff's path) against the tree.\n   - Resolve every target marker R10-ARCH-DOCS-FIRST left. Each named group has landed, so the marker becomes a plain statement of the tree, or is corrected where the landed shape differs from the planned one.\n2. Adjustments: correct the text and regenerate the diagrams wherever the landed shape departs from the target. Each departure is named in the body with the group that caused it.\n3. Wiring test: a tree instrument that resolves every path, instrument, workflow job, event kind and diagram node the docs name, at HEAD. Use brief_lint.mjs or a small checker in the suite's gate.\n   - It goes red on a fixture that renames or removes a named element.\n   - It stays green on a null control.\n   - No unresolved target marker may survive on main.\n\nAlso fold finding P40 (committed card figures not compared to the card), as a check of the committed figures against what they depict.\n\nDiagrams keep the visual language origin/main defines at the base (docs/img/brand/*.svg, docs/site/docs.css, docs/index.html, the card's CSS tokens), read from the tree, light and dark.\n\nIssue #2395. Part of #201.",
